(KESTREL AUTOMATION PVT. LTD.) Tj
T* (EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK - EDITION 2026) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This handbook is a fictional document created for testing a document question-answering system.) Tj
T* (Kestrel Automation Pvt. Ltd. is not a real company.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. INTRODUCTION) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.1 This handbook describes the main workplace policies of Kestrel Automation Pvt. Ltd. \("the) Tj
T* (Company"\). It applies to all full-time employees on the Company payroll. Contractors and) Tj
T* (interns follow the terms written in their individual agreements.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.2 Questions about any policy in this handbook should be sent to the Human Resources \(HR\) team) Tj
T* (at hr@kestrel-automation.example. HR replies to policy questions within 2 working days.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. WORKING HOURS) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.1 The standard working week is 40 hours, from Monday to Friday.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.2 Core working hours are 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on working days. All employees must be) Tj
T* (available for meetings and calls during core hours.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.3 Employees may choose a start time between 8:00 a.m. and 10:00 a.m., provided they complete) Tj
T* (8 working hours each day.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.4 Each working day includes an unpaid lunch break of 45 minutes.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.5 Overtime must be approved in writing by the employee's manager before the work is done.) Tj
T* (Approved overtime is paid at 1.5 times the normal hourly rate, or the employee may choose) Tj
T* (compensatory time off of the same length instead.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3. ANNUAL LEAVE) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.1 Full-time employees receive 20 days of paid annual leave per calendar year.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.2 Annual leave accrues monthly at a rate of 1.67 days per completed month of service.) Tj
T* (Employees who join during the year receive a prorated entitlement for that year.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.3 Requests for annual leave must be submitted through the HR portal at least 14 days before) Tj
T* (the first day of leave.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.4 Leave of more than 10 consecutive working days requires approval from the head of the) Tj
T* (department in addition to the employee's manager.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.5 Up to 5 unused days of annual leave may be carried over to the next calendar year. Carried-) Tj
T* (over days must be used by 31 March of that year, otherwise they expire. Unused days above this) Tj
T* (limit are forfeited and are not paid out.) Tj
T* () Tj
ET
endstream
